id=a52sxq_wallpaper_more
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: more built-in wallpapers (Galaxy S24 Ultra, S26 Ultra, S25, Z Fold8, A52s 5G stock, S7 edge sets)
author=kusti420
description=Adds still images and Samsung Interactive clips from other Galaxy sets to /system/priv-app/wallpaper-res/wallpaper-res.apk, next to the S26U stills and the S24U interactive set of patches/wallpaper_interactive (this patch runs after it under LC_ALL=C sort). Sets (prebuilts/wallpapers/<set>/, PC-side firmware only, nothing of them is flashed): Galaxy S24 Ultra (SM-S928B S928BXXS6EZJ1) 8 stills, Galaxy S26 Ultra (SM-S948B, our base) its 6 interactive clips re-encoded for the SM7325 (patches/wallpaper has to strip the 1440x3120 Main10 90 fps originals), Galaxy S25 (SM-S931B S931BXXUCDZIF) 10 stills and 5 interactive clips, Galaxy Z Fold8 (SM-F976B F976BXXU1AZFW) 4 main-screen stills and its 4 unfold clips (FoldInteractive, hinge-angle driven, useless on a flat phone) recast as interactive clips with a centre 9:20 crop and their own motion table, Galaxy A52s 5G stock One UI 6 (SM-A528B A528BXXU5FWK4) 11 stills, Galaxy S7 edge (SM-G935F G935FXXU8EVG2, framework-res.apk) 8 stock 2016 stills (2240x2240 square like every Samsung still, scaled by the picker). Clips: the S24U recipe (1080x2400 8-bit HEVC Main, 30 fps, every frame a forced IDR_N_LP, CRF 21-22, hvc1), motion tables rescaled by 30/source fps, decoder budget per transition in prebuilts/wallpapers/<set>/README.txt. Stills keep the source square format the picker crops to the screen (S24U 3120 -> 2400x2400 cwebp q95, the rest byte-identical to the source). New resources need new resource ids, so the APK goes through the ROM's apktool flow: DECODE_APK, files into res/raw and res/drawable-nodpi-v4 (all named wpm_*, idempotent), entries appended to res/raw/resources_info.json in the 2.8.78 schema (desc_str_id resolved via getIdentifier with the generic title as fallback, isDefault false everywhere), apktool.yml doNotCompress mp4/webp so the clips stay zip-STORED (openRawResourceFd), and make_rom rebuilds and signs it with the platform key (scripts/apktool.sh, ids of existing resources kept via public.xml).
